<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5917" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bȳzantĭum</span></b> , ii,
			n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βυζάντιον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in Thrace</i>,
				<i>on the Bosphorus</i>, <i>opposite
				the Asiatic Chalcedon</i>, later Constantinopolis, now <i>Constantinople;</i> among the Turks, <i>Istamboul</i> or <i>Stamboul</i>
			(i.e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εις τὴν πόλιν</span>), <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 2,
			6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 11, 18, § 46</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 15, 20, §
			50</span></i> sq.; <i><span class="en">Nep. Paus. 2, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv.
				38, 16, 3 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
				12, 63 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. H. 2</span></i>. 83; 3, 47 al.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bȳzantĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
				Byzantium</i>, <i>Byzantine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litora,</span>”
				<i>the Strait of Constantinople</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 1, 10, 31</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">portus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 15, 20, § 51</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bȳ-zantĭi</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Byzantium</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Prov.
				Cons. 3, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 6</span></i> sq.; <i><span class="en">id. Verr. 2, 2, 31, § 76</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Nep.
				Timoth. 1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 32, 33,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bȳzantĭăcus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of Byzantium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacerti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 4, 9, 13</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bȳzantīnus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., the same (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lygos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Clar. Urb. 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frigora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 7, 17</span></i>
			. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
